Z||000000||LT1 Chop Top||11-18-2001||12:23 AM||||My brother has a 93' 325 BMW that has developed several small cracks in the dash.  What are some of the best products and methods to fix them to restore it to original condition?<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||LawAir||11-18-2001||12:18 PM||||Back In Western New York we used to use toothpaste.  Crest is probably your standard. just apply it above the cracks and then smooth it out with a tongue depressor.  Sometimes colgate makes a good temporary fix.  You can color over the paste once it dries with your favorite crayolas.  <BR>Floss after each use, and see your dentist twice a year!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>My brother has a 93' 325 BMW that has developed several small cracks in the dash.  What are some of the best products and methods to fix them to restore it to original condition?<P>Thanks!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||8
